==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|resipiscence|lang=frm}}, or its source, {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|resipiscentia|lang=la}}, from the present participle of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|resipiscere|resipīscere|to regain consciousness, come to one's senses|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɹɛsᵻˈpɪsn̩s/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|chiefly|_|literary|lang=en}} [[repentance|Repentance]]; recognition of a past mistake, especially with a desire to improve in the future. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}

